languages/sample.zn:1:16: personified-verb: "The record" is not a person or a program and cannot "say"; make the program or person that acts the subject, or use a verb such as "holds", "marks", "declares" or "determines"
languages/sample.zn:1:21: placeholder-noun: "what it is" is a free relative clause; name the exact term instead, such as "the element type" or "the verb's symbol"
languages/sample.zn:1:26: self-reference: the sentence ends on "it is", which points back at its own subject "The record"; end on the new fact instead
languages/sample.zn:4:17: personified-verb: "The flag" is not a person or a program and cannot "decide"; make the program or person that acts the subject, or use a verb such as "holds", "marks", "declares" or "determines"
